abstract: >-
  Data and code behind the post 'Solar drag is uninsurable': satellite lifetime runs under
  storms and a stronger or weaker solar cycle, the 128 published forecasts of Cycle 25, and
  the sunspot record, showing why drag from the solar cycle cannot be insured. Includes the
  article (paper/). Code (scripts/) is MIT; text and figures CC BY 4.0; third-party data under
  its own terms (LICENSE-CONTENT.md): Figure 3 is CC BY-NC 4.0 (WDC-SILSO) and
  data/dst_storm_peaks.csv is for scientific use only (WDC Kyoto).
keywords:
  - space weather
  - atmospheric drag
  - satellite lifetime
  - solar cycle
  - space insurance
